{
 "brief": "Dr. Alaa al-Din al-Akluk, chairman of the National Assembly of Palestinian Tribes, Clans and Families, called for urgent action to restore in-person instruction in Gaza, according to Shehab Wire. He demanded that authorities prepare all necessary conditions to resume the full educational process across the territory.\n\nThe appeal comes as Gaza's school system remains disrupted. Classroom instruction has faced suspension or severe restrictions amid the deteriorating situation on the ground. Tribal and community leaders have increasingly voiced concerns about prolonged gaps in formal education and their impact on students.",
